    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A researcher has two alloys. One alloy contains 90% of gold and the other alloy contains 54% of gold. The researcher mixed 320 grams of the first alloy and 160 grams of the second alloy and obtained the new alloy. What percentage of the gold is contained in the new alloy?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "33%"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "48%"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "65%"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "72%"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "78%"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the grams of gold",
        "body": "Gold in the first alloy: $0.9\\cdot 320 = 288$ g. In the second: $0.54\\cdot 160 = 86.4$ g. Total gold: $374.4$ g in $480$ g of alloy.\n\n$\\frac{374.4}{480} = 0.78 = 78\\%$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 78%**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Weighted average",
        "body": "The first alloy is twice as heavy as the second, so the new percentage is the weighted average $\\frac{2\\cdot 90 + 1\\cdot 54}{3} = \\frac{234}{3} = 78\\%$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 78%**"
      }
    ],
