      {
        "title": "Set up an equation",
        "body": "Let Carl be $c$ now; his brothers are $c - 2$ and $c - 4$. In three years Mary is 51 and the sons are $c+3$, $c+1$, $c-1$, with sum $3c + 3$.\n\n$3c + 3 = 51$ gives $c = 16$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 16**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Use the middle son",
        "body": "In three years the three sons' ages are evenly spaced, so their sum is 3 times the middle son's age: the middle son will be $51 / 3 = 17$, and Carl will be 19. So Carl is $19 - 3 = 16$ now.\n\n**Answer: (B) 16**"
      }
