        "body": "The contents are: one box with 10 red, one with 10 green and one mixed box (15 red and 15 green in total).\n\nTry one pen from the box labelled \"5 red, 5 green\". This label is wrong, so that box is all red or all green, and one pen tells which. Say it's red. Then the box labelled \"10 green\" is not green and not red (red is taken), so it is the mixed box, and the box labelled \"10 red\" holds the green pens. (If the pen is green, the argument is symmetric.)\n\nWith 0 pens we can't decide, since two arrangements are possible. So 1 pen is the minimum.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
